 and node3 (both share subnet 10.100.147.0/24 with node1) using iptables DROP rules on each host targeting the other host's IP, while leaving node1 (and gateway) traffic unaffected. Rules persisted via iptables-openrc. Completed the mandatory single-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes with confirmed boot-identity changes and full post-restart recovery of both connectivity and isolation.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Surveyed topology: node1 (SONiC/Debian), node2 and node3 (Alpine), all sharing subnet 10.100.147.0/24\",\"Found baseline violation: node2 and node3 could ping each other directly; node1 initially unreachable due to a stalled DHCP lease on eth0\",\"Diagnosed and resolved node1 connectivity: confirmed eth0 (not eth1) is the correct shared-segment interface; DHCP subsequently succeeded, assigning 10.100.147.10\",\"Installed iptables via apk on node2 and node3 (not present by default on Alpine)\",\"Added rules on node2: DROP INPUT from 10.100.147.12 and DROP OUTPUT to 10.100.147.12 (node3's IP)\",\"Added rules on node3: DROP INPUT from 10.100.147.11 and DROP OUTPUT to 10.100.147.11 (node2's IP)\",\"Verified node2<->node3 traffic blocked while both still reach node1 and the gateway\",\"Persisted rules via rc-update add iptables default and iptables save; verified reload via rc-service iptables restart\",\"Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime, connectivity, firewall state) on all three nodes\",\"Restarted node2 via reboot; polled until exec available; confirmed new boot_id; verified persisted iptables rules and correct isolation/connectivity\",\"Restarted node3 via reboot; polled until exec available; confirmed new boot_id; verified persisted iptables rules and correct isolation/connectivity\",\"Restarted node1 via systemctl reboot (first background attempt did not trigger; foreground command succeeded); polled until exec available; confirmed new boot_id; verified DHCP re-acquired 10.100.147.10 and connectivity to node2/node3 restored\",\"Final cross-check on node2 and node3 confirmed isolation and node1 reachability intact after all three restarts\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"Baseline: node2/node3 could talk directly before fix, node1 baseline health\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-9fa933546d7a4af7\",\"cmd-d1a46ccacdf54998\",\"cmd-0140f5c1dd3d4c4f\"],\"summary\":\"node2 pinged node3 successfully (violating isolation) while node1's eth0 initially had no working address; later confirmed eth0 is the correct interface with working connectivity to both node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2/node3 mutual isolation implemented and verified\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-f069b04a60484095\",\"cmd-6744dd4b1f4847f4\",\"cmd-6c4de53b2ea94f23\",\"cmd-b84deb9d54f34920\"],\"summary\":\"iptables DROP rules added on node2 (blocking 10.100.147.12) and node3 (blocking 10.100.147.11); ping tests show 'Operation not permitted' between node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 both still reach node1 after isolation\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6c4de53b2ea94f23\",\"cmd-b84deb9d54f34920\"],\"summary\":\"node2->node1 and node3->node1 pings succeed (0% loss) while gateway reachability also confirmed\"},{\"requirement\":\"Isolation rules persisted across reboot\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-3f8db8ad0a644177\",\"cmd-5f29add09a0d454c\",\"cmd-eb4145a962fa4550\",\"cmd-407eb832ee3e4c7c\"],\"summary\":\"iptables-openrc enabled and rules saved to /etc/iptables/rules-save on node2/node3; rc-service iptables restart reloads identical DROP rules from disk\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-a39d28342f064f03\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node2 boot_id (547e44e4...), uptime, and firewall rules prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-537acfde6888460d\",\"cmd-54e6e4f8bb77488a\"],\"summary\":\"reboot command caused stream disconnect (acknowledgement); subsequent poll shows new boot_id f3f80661... and uptime 16.74s, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 post-restart recovery (connectivity + isolation)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-436eb56b10dd4f81\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, node2 iptables DROP rules present, ping to node1 succeeds, ping to node3 blocked with 'Operation not permitted'\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-4e780dd3cacd4869\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node3 boot_id (c331951f...), uptime, and firewall rules prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e020bfd0a7b5499b\",\"cmd-357e09aa74554aea\"],\"summary\":\"reboot command caused stream disconnect; subsequent poll shows new boot_id dae2038e... and uptime 20.41s, proving an actual reboot occurred\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 post-restart recovery (connectivity + isolation)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-e101142094fe4ed7\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, node3 iptables DROP rules present, ping to node1 succeeds, ping to node2 blocked with 'Operation not permitted'\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 healthy baseline before restart\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-2b733436e6e14641\"],\"summary\":\"Captured node1 boot_id (34192023...), uptime, eth0 address, and successful pings to node2 and node3 prior to restart\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 restart acknowledgement and changed boot identity\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-badb1bb7825946fc\",\"cmd-099fca01ac414af6\"],\"summary\":\"systemctl reboot caused connection reset (acknowledgement); subsequent poll shows new boot_id 1b86c994... and uptime 10.38s, proving an actual reboot occurred (initial backgrounded 'reboot' attempt did not trigger a real reboot, confirmed by unchanged boot_id in cmd-5a8ada5839964bc0, so systemctl reboot was used instead)\"},{\"requirement\":\"node1 post-restart recovery (connectivity)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-907b21abf2eb4a5f\"],\"summary\":\"After reboot, node1 eth0 re-acquired 10.100.147.10 via DHCP and successfully pinged both node2 and node3\"},{\"requirement\":\"Final full-cluster verification: isolation and connectivity both intact after all three restarts\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-ba82405071334b2e\",\"cmd-b541adfa06cb44ad\"],\"summary\":\"node2 and node3 confirmed still blocked from each other ('Operation not permitted') while both still reach node1 (0% packet loss); DROP rules confirmed present on both hosts\"}]}","structured_output":{"status":"completed","summary":"Implemented host-based port isolation between node2 and node3 (both share subnet 10.100.147.0/24 with node1) using iptables DROP rules on each host targeting the other host's IP, while leaving node1 (and gateway) traffic unaffected. Rules persisted via iptables-openrc. Completed the mandatory single-node-at-a-time restart protocol on all three nodes with confirmed boot-identity changes and full post-restart recovery of both connectivity and isolation.","actions_performed":["Surveyed topology: node1 (SONiC/Debian), node2 and node3 (Alpine), all sharing subnet 10.100.147.0/24","Found baseline violation: node2 and node3 could ping each other directly; node1 initially unreachable due to a stalled DHCP lease on eth0","Diagnosed and resolved node1 connectivity: confirmed eth0 (not eth1) is the correct shared-segment interface; DHCP subsequently succeeded, assigning 10.100.147.10","Installed iptables via apk on node2 and node3 (not present by default on Alpine)","Added rules on node2: DROP INPUT from 10.100.147.12 and DROP OUTPUT to 10.100.147.12 (node3's IP)","Added rules on node3: DROP INPUT from 10.100.147.11 and DROP OUTPUT to 10.100.147.11 (node2's IP)","Verified node2<->node3 traffic blocked while both still reach node1 and the gateway","Persisted rules via rc-update add iptables default and iptables save; verified reload via rc-service iptables restart","Captured pre-restart baseline (boot_id, uptime, connectivity, firewall state) on all three nodes","Restarted node2 via reboot; polled until exec available; confirmed new boot_id; verified persisted iptables rules and correct isolation/connectivity","Restarted node3 via reboot; polled until exec available; confirmed new boot_id; verified persisted iptables rules and correct isolation/connectivity","Restarted node1 via systemctl reboot (first background attempt did not trigger; foreground command succeeded); polled until exec available; confirmed new boot_id; verified DHCP re-acquired 10.100.147.10 and connectivity to node2/node3 restored","Final cross-check on node2 and node3 confirmed isolation and node1 reachability intact after all three restarts"],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Baseline: node2/node3 could talk directly before fix, node1 baseline health","command_ids":["cmd-9fa933546d7a4af7","cmd-d1a46ccacdf54998","cmd-0140f5c1dd3d4c4f"],"summary":"node2 pinged node3 successfully (violating isolation) while node1's eth0 initially had no working address; later confirmed eth0 is the correct interface with working connectivity to both node2 and node3"},{"requirement":"node2/node3 mutual isolation implemented and verified","command_ids":["cmd-f069b04a60484095","cmd-6744dd4b1f4847f4","cmd-6c4de53b2ea94f23","cmd-b84deb9d54f34920"],"summary":"iptables DROP rules added on node2 (blocking 10.100.147.12) and node3 (blocking 10.100.147.11); ping tests show 'Operation not permitted' between node2 and node3"},{"requirement":"node2 and node3 both still reach node1 after isolation","command_ids":["cmd-6c4de53b2ea94f23","cmd-b84deb9d54f34920"],"summary":"node2->node1 and node3->node1 pings succeed (0% loss) while gateway reachability also confirmed"},{"requirement":"Isolation rules persisted across reboot","command_ids":["cmd-3f8db8ad0a644177","cmd-5f29add09a0d454c","cmd-eb4145a962fa4550","cmd-407eb832ee3e4c7c"],"summary":"iptables-openrc enabled and rules saved to /etc/iptables/rules-save on node2/node3; rc-service iptables restart reloads identical DROP rules from disk"},{"requirement":"node2 healthy baseline before restart","command_ids":["cmd-a39d2834